userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the global-admin `/admin/skills` page with the `useSkillCatalog` composable and an Add-source dialog.

**Motivation** — Global admins need a UI to register, update and remove skill sources and see each source's pinned commit, status and skills.

**Approach**

- `composables/useSkillCatalog.ts`: `list()`, `create({ gitUrl, ref, path })`, `update(id)`, `remove(id)` via `useApi()` on the admin routes (`GET /admin/skills/sources` returning the response's `items`; `POST /admin/skills/sources` with JSON body `{ gitUrl, ref, path }`; `POST /admin/skills/sources/:id/update`; `DELETE /admin/skills/sources/:id`). Pattern: `apps/web/composables/useFleetRepos.ts`.
- `pages/admin/skills.vue` (global admins; a 403 from `list()` sets `adminOnly` and renders the `skills.adminOnly` note, as `pages/admin/fleet/repos.vue` does): table of sources (URL, ref, short SHA (first 7 characters) or `—` when `resolvedSha` is null, path, status badge with reason, skill count) with Add (dialog, vee-validate + zod: `gitUrl` must match `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>`, `ref` required, `path` optional), Update, Remove (confirm; confirm-dialog and toast patterns from `components/ProjectMembersPanel.vue`), and an expandable row listing each skill's name and description.
- `components/AddSkillSourceDialog.vue`: the Add dialog. An empty path field submits `path: ''`. On a `create` rejection (e.g. 409) it shows a toast with the message from `extractApiError` and stays open.
- i18n keys in `i18n/locales/en.json` and `zh.json` (namespace `skills`: page, table headers, form incl. `skills.form.gitUrlInvalid`, `skills.adminOnly`, status/actions/confirm). Both locale files change together (locale-parity tests compare key sets). `nav.skills` and `skills.project.*` keys are added by US-007. The web app uses Nuxt-native composables for API access, not a generated client; business rules stay in the API.

SEAM-3 (US-003, US-004 -> US-006): the admin routes are consumed by `useSkillCatalog`; ACs assert the request path and the JSON body `{ gitUrl, ref, path }`.

Failure handling (web): create 409 -> toast with `extractApiError`, dialog stays open; list 403 -> `skills.adminOnly` note, no Add button; `RESOLVE_FAILED` -> failure badge including `statusReason`.

**Scope** — In: `useSkillCatalog`, `pages/admin/skills.vue`, `AddSkillSourceDialog.vue`, en/zh `skills` admin keys, specs. Out: project Skills tab, `ProjectSkillsPanel`, Switch component, `nav.skills` link, command-palette entry (US-007). Feature-level: no CLI commands; no editing or authoring of skill content.

**Interface**
```ts
// composables/useSkillCatalog.ts
export function useSkillCatalog(): {
  list(): Promise<SkillSourceDto[]>
  create(input: { gitUrl: string; path: string; ref: string }): Promise<SkillSourceDto>
  update(id: string): Promise<SkillSourceDto>
  remove(id: string): Promise<void>
}
// SkillSourceDto: { id, gitUrl, ref, path, resolvedSha, resolvedAt, status, statusReason, createdAt, skills: SkillDto[] }
// SkillDto: { id, name, description, dir }
```
